Subject: [PATCH] ctrl: each DataElements getter resolves its rows against the rows its table lists, and reads nothing it did not find

A single-parameter GET read a row that is not there:
- a BSS on a device without BSSs through an uninitialised pointer;
- the radio m_radio[n - 1] for any n (0 and aliases m_radio[-1], past the radio count a stale
  slot, past 3 outside the array);
- Network.SSID.0 at get_network_ssid(UINT_MAX);
- past the last BSS, or an alias with no match, the last row it looked at.

The wf6ap and wf7ap getters took the second model whatever its instance. The STA MLD lookup
counted the STA MLDs of the other AP MLDs, one off, and the STA MLD and affiliated STA counters
came from the first other STA. The policy getter read the first policy whatever its type. The
network's ControllerID, ColocatedAgentID, TimeStamp and SSIDs came from the list's first model,
which may be an agent's. A device row could be the controller's own model, whose instance number
was never set.

Now one helper per table level returns NULL for 0, past the last row or an alias with no match,
and each getter returns an error before it reads:
- the device rows device_tget_inner lists;
- the radio rows 1 to the radio count;
- the BSS rows bss_tget_params lists, the radio's BSSs with a BSSID;
- the STA MLD rows of their AP MLD.

The network's values come from the controller's own model, and the policy getter reads the
Default 802.1Q Settings policy. The affiliated AP and STA indexes are bounded by their arrays,
and a model's instance is -1 until it is set. The method handlers that use the radio and BSS
helpers get NULL instead of a wrong row.

Unit tests (em_ctrl_t_de_getters, 8): pass on this change; on the code before it all 8 fail, and
UBSan reports m_radio[-1] and m_network_ssid[4294967295].
